35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: The bus links in the outer wards are gone. Residents now face an hour's round trip to reach any staffed counter.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,- **Rin**: The old outreach stops had forty visitors a session! That is way more than the main building gets.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: The grant covers fees for twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs them. The vehicle line also overran by a third.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"- **Minako**: The volunteer register shows retired tradespeople running repair clinics, but no one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: The winter closures shut roads for eleven days, yet the community halls kept their evening timetables running without interruption.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, that confirms my fear. If the halls stay open, our fixed hours and locations are the real barrier, not the weather.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Benjamin, wait! The old digitisation project left half its images unindexed. We can’t just trust the records!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the unindexed images are a cautionary tale, but the grant’s twelve-month cliff is the immediate financial threat.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle overrun is a warning, but my concern is the supervision gap. We cannot manage external partners without trained staff.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Jonathan, I see your point. The halls prove that community will persists even when our infrastructure fails.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, exactly. The community will is there, but our rigid locations and hours are the bottleneck. We must rethink access.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, that supervision gap is scary! But the partner groups from six years ago still meet without help. Maybe we don’t need to supervise everything?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, that is a dangerous assumption. Unsupervised success is luck, not a model. I need to know if the funding can sustain the oversight we actually require.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, self-sustaining groups are rare exceptions, not a strategy. We need a reliable roster of trained supervisors to ensure consistency and safety.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Minako, I agree. We must not rely on luck. Let us ensure our plans account for the gaps in our current capabilities.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, agreed. We must design for the reality of who can reach us, not just what we wish to offer.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, but the old stops worked because they came to us! If we go to them, we fix the bus problem too.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, mobility solves access, but the vehicle line overran by a third. I need to know if the grant covers that recurring cost before we commit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle overrun is a real risk, but the supervision gap is immediate. We cannot hire drivers if we cannot manage the staff who run the stops.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
