60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are A: Mobile Branch Service, B: Maker Workshop, C: Language Learning Circles, and D: Digital Archive Portal.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, the Mobile Branch Service directly addresses the access gap I identified. It brings the service to those cut off by the bus rerouting.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Jonathan, yes! The Mobile Branch is like the old stops that actually worked! I want to vote for A!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, enthusiasm is noted, but the vehicle line overran by a third. I need to see if the grant covers that recurring cost before we commit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle cost is a concern, but the supervision gap is immediate. We lack trained staff to manage the external partners required for the other options.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Minako, the Mobile Branch uses our own staff, so it avoids the supervision gap you fear.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, precisely. It relies on our existing infrastructure and staff, avoiding the external dependencies that plague the other options.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Shizue, that makes sense! If we use our own people, we don’t have to worry about the missing supervisors.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, that is a fair point, but the vehicle line overran by a third. I need to know if the grant covers that recurring cost before we commit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the grant covers session fees, not vehicle maintenance. The overrun is a recurring risk, but the Mobile Branch still avoids the external supervision gap I flagged.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Minako, you are right. The Mobile Branch keeps us in control of our own people and schedule, which feels safest.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, agreed. It restores access to the outer wards without relying on external partners or fragile funding structures.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Benjamin, but the old stops proved people will come! The vehicle cost is just a number we can fix later.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, ""fix later"" is how budgets die. The grant ends in twelve months, and the vehicle line is already over. I cannot vote for a recurring cost we cannot sustain.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I hear your caution, but the supervision gap makes the other options impossible right now. The Mobile Branch is the only one we can actually staff safely today.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,- **Shizue**: I am ready to vote. The Mobile Branch seems the most stable path forward for our community.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. The Mobile Branch restores access to the outer wards without relying on external partners or fragile funding structures.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I vote for A! The old stops worked, and this brings the library to us!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I vote for A. The access gap is critical, and while the vehicle costs worry me, the other options carry risks I cannot accept.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for A. It is the only option we can staff safely today without the supervision gap I identified.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
